1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,110
Repair technicians hunt for faults on logic boards under a microscope.

2
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:10,008
Glare, blur and leads half a millimetre apart turn every photo into a guess.

3
00:00:11,308 --> 00:00:12,438
This is BoardGuard:

4
00:00:12,438 --> 00:00:15,831
an AI microscope assistant that knows when to look again.

5
00:00:17,631 --> 00:00:21,057
It runs a real perception, decision and action loop.

6
00:00:21,057 --> 00:00:23,100
OpenCV 5 measures the evidence.

7
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:25,868
An agent applies explicit, testable rules.

8
00:00:25,868 --> 00:00:30,942
And when the evidence is weak, it asks for a better look instead of guessing.

9
00:00:32,742 --> 00:00:34,263
This is the live app.

10
00:00:34,263 --> 00:00:39,551
The 3D board is for navigation, and every region links to real microscope

11
00:00:39,551 --> 00:00:40,202
captures.

12
00:00:40,202 --> 00:00:41,072
Scenario 02:

13
00:00:41,072 --> 00:00:44,113
a fine-pitch TQFP chip under a ring light.

14
00:00:45,818 --> 00:00:51,945
OpenCV 5 checks the image quality, then finds two suspected solder bridges.

15
00:00:51,945 --> 00:00:55,132
But C01 sits inside a specular hotspot:

16
00:00:55,132 --> 00:00:57,337
28% of its region is glare.

17
00:00:57,935 --> 00:01:00,871
Technicians can check any region themselves.

18
00:01:00,871 --> 00:01:04,741
Press R, drag a box, and BoardGuard measures glare, focus,

19
00:01:04,741 --> 00:01:07,477
exposure and lead resolution right there.

20
00:01:07,477 --> 00:01:08,011
Verdict:

21
00:01:08,011 --> 00:01:08,879
insufficient.

22
00:01:09,577 --> 00:01:11,598
So the agent will not decide.

23
00:01:11,598 --> 00:01:14,943
Rule R-E1 requests one specific new observation:

24
00:01:14,943 --> 00:01:16,894
diffuse light, same framing.

25
00:01:20,495 --> 00:01:22,401
The technician recaptures.

26
00:01:22,401 --> 00:01:26,212
SIFT and MAGSAC register the new image to the first,

27
00:01:26,212 --> 00:01:28,777
and every finding is checked again.

28
00:01:28,777 --> 00:01:32,075
C01 is not reproduced, so its priority drops.

29
00:01:32,075 --> 00:01:33,028
C02 persists:

30
00:01:33,028 --> 00:01:35,300
a fibre lying across two leads.

31
00:01:35,959 --> 00:01:37,256
Need real dimensions?

32
00:01:37,256 --> 00:01:41,456
Calibrate from the detected lead row with the package pitch, 0.5 mm,

33
00:01:41,456 --> 00:01:43,618
and the ruler reads in millimetres.

34
00:01:44,322 --> 00:01:46,407
The technician makes the call.

35
00:01:46,407 --> 00:01:47,241
Dismiss C01.

36
00:01:47,241 --> 00:01:48,492
Changed your mind?

37
00:01:48,492 --> 00:01:51,829
Undo it, and the withdrawal stays on the record.

38
00:01:51,829 --> 00:01:55,860
Confirm C02, and BoardGuard recommends a continuity check.

39
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:57,250
It never claims one.

40
00:01:57,923 --> 00:02:02,510
Every tool call, rule and human decision is traced, timed and exportable.

41
00:02:08,585 --> 00:02:12,687
After the repair, BoardGuard registers the before and after captures,

42
00:02:12,687 --> 00:02:16,372
maps what changed, and links that change back to each finding.

43
00:02:16,886 --> 00:02:18,499
Visible change documented.

44
00:02:18,499 --> 00:02:21,601
Electrical verification stays with the technician.

45
00:02:27,423 --> 00:02:30,224
And when two photos cannot be aligned reliably,

46
00:02:30,224 --> 00:02:32,906
BoardGuard says so and withholds the overlay.

47
00:02:34,543 --> 00:02:40,196
Under the hood, the Next.js workstation calls a FastAPI service on AWS Lambda

48
00:02:40,196 --> 00:02:41,885
through a Function URL.

49
00:02:41,885 --> 00:02:45,996
The agent and every OpenCV 5 pipeline run inside Lambda.

50
00:02:45,996 --> 00:02:51,209
Evidence goes to a private, encrypted S3 bucket, logs go to CloudWatch,

51
00:02:51,209 --> 00:02:54,660
and one CloudFormation template deploys it all.

52
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:58,756
The System screen shows it live:

53
00:02:58,756 --> 00:03:03,216
OpenCV 5.0.0 running on AWS Lambda, with a real processing probe.

54
00:03:07,782 --> 00:03:09,158
And we measured it.

55
00:03:09,158 --> 00:03:12,419
Registration succeeded on all 81 known warps,

56
00:03:12,419 --> 00:03:17,852
with a median corner error of 0.09 px, and rejected all 23 unrelated pairs.

57
00:03:17,852 --> 00:03:21,910
On 10 synthetic glare cases, a single image got 5 wrong.

58
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:25,387
After one targeted recapture, all 10 were right.

59
00:03:25,387 --> 00:03:30,459
9 of 9 agent scenarios passed, with zero unsafe automatic conclusions.

60
00:03:32,159 --> 00:03:36,575
BoardGuard is not an electrical tester, and not a validated diagnostic.

61
00:03:36,575 --> 00:03:40,308
It is a visual inspection aid that knows when to look again.

62
00:03:41,908 --> 00:03:47,071
Built by team BoardGuard for the OpenCV AI Competition 2026.
